silm:instances_papers_11_base_commutative_diagram_chapters_05_relator_quotient_projection_sections_02_quotient_projection_pi_dissection_concrete_anchor_20_ValidationShape#validationshape silm:hasLongDescription "The ValidationShape is the SHACL-style shape checking the path law c=r.a on Mittens-records. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'ValidationShape', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
